- If the tree is empty, return 0.
- Recursively find the depth of the left subtree.
- Then, find the depth of the right subtree.
- Compare both depths using Math.max().
- Add 1 for the current node.
Time Complexity: O(n)

Each node is visited once. To determine the maximum depth, all nodes in the tree must be checked.

Space Complexity: O(h), where h is the height of the tree. This space is used by the recursion stack.
For a balanced tree, the recursion depth is O(log n); however, the O(n) time complexity cannot be improved, as the entire tree must be examined.
